{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/673885-can-wraiths-teach-themselves-arcanois","id":673885,"title":"Can Wraiths teach themselves Arcanois?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-21T23:25:15-07:00","id":673885,"title":"Can Wraiths teach themselves Arcanois?","content":"Some of the books talk about how some guilds keep a lock on the upper levels of their Arcanos, but can a Wraith just teach him or herself Arcanois without help from other Wraiths? What can a Wraith do in her own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T04:58:05-07:00","id":674061,"title":"","content":"Presumably someone had to at least once. It's probably more difficult, and you might end up with a variant, a more obvious Arcanos marking, and a visit from the guild in question, but it should be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T09:47:40-07:00","id":674353,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">RAW:<br /> No idea<br /> <br /> Me:<br /> I\u2019d allow it, if it made sense for the character. A habitual jogger developing Argos, a bouncer developing Outrage, or an accountant developing Usury all make sense. Depending on the story (and the player), characters may need help from a Guild to learn the upper echelons of their abilities.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:09:42-07:00","id":674760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/673885-can-wraiths-teach-themselves-arcanois?p=674353#post674353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">. . . I\u2019d allow it, if it made sense for the character. A habitual jogger developing Argos, a bouncer developing Outrage, or an accountant developing Usury all make sense. Depending on the story (and the player), characters may need help from a Guild to learn the upper echelons of their abilities.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the impression I've always gotten. Wraith abilities are (at least partially) based on what they believe ghosts can do, and a number of books (describing character creation) talk about new wraiths getting arcanoi that make inherent &quot;sense&quot; to the character. A plastic surgeon (or s/fx makeup artist) is likely to develop Moliate (shapeshifting), a psychotherapist Castigate (which suppresses the Shadow) . . .<br /> <br /> However, I've never seen (explicitly) whether its purely personal preference and effort (the shrink deliberately trying to learn Castigate, for example), or whether they posses an inherent/instinctive grasp of the Arcanos. Given what they are though, the instinctive approach does make some sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: For some of those powers, though, I'd really want a teacher - fooling around with them on your own seems dangerous. Destroying souls, warding against Spectres, casting people into the Tempest . . . at some point, getting a Guild tutor makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 09-22-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T00:04:15-07:00","id":674971,"title":"","content":"Well, if nothing else, I suppose there is always the Pact of Doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T20:37:37-07:00","id":675987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/673885-can-wraiths-teach-themselves-arcanois?p=674061#post674061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably someone had to at least once.</div> </div> </div> </div>This ^<br /> Someone invented these powers. However, one could make an argument that someone trying to independently invent the powers should cost much more XP. It's a lot harder to invent a car when all you can see is the outside, versus actually being trained on how to build a car.<br /> <br /> Of course, for the simple sake of playability, I wouldn't make it cost a realistic amount more. (A realistic amount more being 10+ times the cost) Maybe just 1.5 times the XP of being taught.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T11:25:56-07:00","id":677823,"title":"","content":"It really depends on how strict one wants to be as a Storyteller, what the themes and moods of the game in question are, things like that. Just going by the established fiction, yes, wraiths can reach the higher levels of Arcanoi without any outside influence. Whether it's unconsciously tapping into the Shadow's Hive-Mind connection to pull the information, or pulling from the ephemera of the Tempest, or even spontaneously developing, the narrative allows for it. Instead, Guilds make it easier and more apparent on how to progress in Arcanoi, and often provide tutelage, but their real power lies in creating a powerful economic bloc, or a community to share and swap stories and techniques, along with prestige and protection the Guild name provides. A troupe of highly-advertised, Guild-sanctioned Sandmen will play to larger and more powerful audiences than the guy that taught himself, and a concentrated group of Artificers will undertake more impressive projects than the dude next door.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}